{"seq":18,"slug":"evolutionary-psychology","title":"进化心理学","stage":"DONE","category":"psychology","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology","rating":{"composite":3.79,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4,"strategic":3.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.11,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":2.5}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"进化心理学-简介\">进化心理学 简介</h1><p>进化心理学（Evolutionary Psychology）是将达尔文自然选择理论应用于人类心理与行为研究的学科分支。它试图回答一个根本性问题：为什么人类会以特定方式思考、感受和行动？与描述「是什么」「怎么样」的多数心理学分支不同，进化心理学追问的是<strong>终极原因（ultimate cause）</strong>——某一心理特征在祖先环境中解决了什么适应性问题、为何被自然选择保留至今。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-与兄弟-hub-的分工\">本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工</h2><p>进化心理学位于心理学知识库的第 18 章，与多个兄弟 hub 互补而不重叠。下表明确各自边界，避免在本 hub 重复展开属于他人的内容：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>关注问题</th>\n<th>本 hub（进化心理学）</th>\n<th>兄弟 hub</th>\n<th>边界</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>终极原因（为何演化出此机制）</td>\n<td>✅ 核心</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>本 hub 专属视角</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>近端机制（神经/激素如何实现）</td>\n<td>引用，不展开</td>\n<td><a href=\"../biological-psychology/\"><code>02_biological-psychology</code></a>、<a href=\"../neuropsychology/\"><code>17_neuropsychology</code></a></td>\n<td>脑区、神经递质细节去神经类 hub</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>群体与态度（偏见、从众、群际）</td>\n<td>进化解释</td>\n<td><a href=\"../social-psychology/\"><code>05_social-psychology</code></a></td>\n<td>社会层面机制去社会心理学</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>障碍的诊断与治疗</td>\n<td>进化重诠释</td>\n<td><a href=\"../clinical-abnormal-psychology/\"><code>09_clinical-abnormal-psychology</code></a></td>\n<td>临床实务去临床 hub</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>发展阶段与认知里程碑</td>\n<td>生活史/关键期</td>\n<td><a href=\"../developmental-psychology/\"><code>04_developmental-psychology</code></a></td>\n<td>常规发展描述去发展 hub</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>一句话区分：兄弟 hub 回答<strong>机制如何运作</strong>与<strong>现象是什么</strong>，本 hub 回答<strong>它为什么会存在</strong>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"适合读者与前置\">适合读者与前置</h2><p>本 hub 适合对人类行为终极原因感兴趣的读者：心理学研究者、生物学爱好者、社会科学从业者，以及希望从进化视角理解日常行为的学习者。建议前置：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>必备</strong>：基础心理学概论（实体名、研究范式）、生物进化论常识（自然选择、遗传、变异）。</li>\n<li><strong>推荐</strong>：博弈论入门（理解互惠、合作的演化稳定性），统计直觉（理解效应量、跨文化方差）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"全书结构\">全书结构</h2><p>全书分四章，层层递进：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>章</th>\n<th>主题</th>\n<th>回答的核心问题</th>\n<th>关键理论/人物</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>一</td>\n<td><a href=\"theoretical-foundations/\">理论基础</a></td>\n<td>心理特征如何被选择塑造？</td>\n<td>达尔文、Williams、Hamilton、Tooby &amp; Cosmides</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>二</td>\n<td><a href=\"survival-and-mating/\">生存与择偶</a></td>\n<td>两性繁殖策略为何分化？</td>\n<td>Trivers、Buss、Singh</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>三</td>\n<td><a href=\"social-cognition/\">社会认知</a></td>\n<td>大规模合作如何可能？</td>\n<td>Trivers、Axelrod、Fehr、Tajfel</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>四</td>\n<td><a href=\"modern-applications/\">现代应用</a></td>\n<td>古老心理在现代如何失配？</td>\n<td>Nesse、Miller、Li</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"flowchart\" data-source=\"flowchart LR&#10;    A[第一章 理论基础&lt;br/&gt;选择·适应·机制] --&gt; B[第二章 生存与择偶&lt;br/&gt;亲代投资·性选择]&#10;    A --&gt; C[第三章 社会认知&lt;br/&gt;合作·欺骗·联盟]&#10;    B --&gt; D[第四章 现代应用&lt;br/&gt;临床·消费·失配]&#10;    C --&gt; D&#10;    A -.贯穿全书的方法论.-&gt; D\">flowchart LR\n    A[第一章 理论基础&lt;br/&gt;选择·适应·机制] --&gt; B[第二章 生存与择偶&lt;br/&gt;亲代投资·性选择]\n    A --&gt; C[第三章 社会认知&lt;br/&gt;合作·欺骗·联盟]\n    B --&gt; D[第四章 现代应用&lt;br/&gt;临床·消费·失配]\n    C --&gt; D\n    A -.贯穿全书的方法论.-&gt; D</pre><h2 id=\"推荐学习路径\">推荐学习路径</h2><ol>\n<li><strong>打地基</strong>：先通读第一章三节，掌握「自然选择→适应→进化心理机制」这条主线与适应主义方法论。其中 <a href=\"theoretical-foundations/natural-selection-and-adaptation\">Hamilton 规则</a>、<a href=\"theoretical-foundations/evolved-psychological-mechanisms\">领域特异性</a> 是后续各章反复调用的基础概念。</li>\n<li><strong>按兴趣分流</strong>：关注两性、亲密关系→第二章；关注合作、信任、群体→第三章。两章相对独立，可任选其一深入。</li>\n<li><strong>看现实意义</strong>：第四章把前三章的理论延伸到临床、消费与公共健康，建议最后阅读以形成闭环。</li>\n<li><strong>时间有限</strong>：优先读每章第一节即可获得核心概念全景；<a href=\"modern-applications/evolutionary-mismatch\">进化失配</a> 是把整套理论串起来的最佳单篇总结。</li>\n</ol>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"theoretical-foundations","title":"理论基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/theoretical-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"natural-selection-and-adaptation","title":"自然选择与适应","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/theoretical-foundations/natural-selection-and-adaptation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"evolved-psychological-mechanisms","title":"进化心理机制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/theoretical-foundations/evolved-psychological-mechanisms"},{"seq":3,"slug":"phylogeny-and-ontogeny","title":"种系发生与个体发生","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/theoretical-foundations/phylogeny-and-ontogeny"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"survival-and-mating","title":"生存与择偶","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/survival-and-mating","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"mate-selection-strategies","title":"择偶策略","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/survival-and-mating/mate-selection-strategies"},{"seq":2,"slug":"parental-investment-theory","title":"亲代投资理论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/survival-and-mating/parental-investment-theory"},{"seq":3,"slug":"intrasexual-competition","title":"同性竞争与性别差异","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/survival-and-mating/intrasexual-competition"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"social-cognition","title":"社会认知","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/social-cognition","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"cooperation-and-altruism","title":"合作与利他行为","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/social-cognition/cooperation-and-altruism"},{"seq":2,"slug":"cheater-detection-and-trust","title":"欺骗检测与信任","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/social-cognition/cheater-detection-and-trust"},{"seq":3,"slug":"coalitional-psychology","title":"联盟心理学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/evolutionary-psychology/social-cognition/coalitional-psychology"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"m